# Trivy vulnerability exceptions
#
# Scope: these four findings ONLY. Any other HIGH/CRITICAL finding still fails the
# "Docker build + scan" job in .github/workflows/application-ci.yml.
#
# All four are transitive Go dependencies compiled into the upstream FrankenPHP
# binary (usr/local/bin/frankenphp) via Caddy's certmagic/smallstep (ACME CA) and
# OpenTelemetry OTLP exporter chains — not Laravel/Composer application dependencies,
# and not something this repo's Dockerfile/Caddy config can patch directly.
#
# Investigated 2026-08-29: no patched FrankenPHP release exists yet. Checked both the
# latest release (v1.12.7, 2026-08-07) and the unreleased `main` branch — both still
# pin github.com/getkin/kin-openapi v0.140.0 and google.golang.org/grpc v1.81.1.
#
# Reachability: this deployment runs `frankenphp php-server` with no custom Caddyfile
# and no OTLP/ACME/xDS/gRPC configuration anywhere in deploy/ or scripts/ (TLS is
# terminated by ingress-nginx, not Caddy). The vulnerable code paths are compiled in
# but not invoked by this application.
#
# Review by: 2026-09-28 (30 days). Re-run `docker build` + Trivy against the latest
# dunglas/frankenphp:1-php8.4-alpine on or before this date; remove any entry once a
# release fixes it, and re-investigate/extend only with a documented reason if not.

# kin-openapi: ValidationHandler.Load() Fail-Open (fixed upstream in 0.144.0)
